      "content": "helped to know what the textbooks say. but im still a bit stuck on the \"correct\" part of my first question. if im trying to raise my kid to be prepared for the real world, shouldn't i be teaching them the most established medical and scientific facts? if some doctors or researchers disagree with the idea that gender is fluid, shouldn't i at least mention that to my kid so they aren't confused when they hear it elsewhere? or is the \"correct\" way to just focus on the inclusive side?",
